<article class="env-remark" id="06JB">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06JB">Remark <span data-tag="06JB">9.4.5.6</span>.</a> In the situation of Theorem <a data-tag="06J9" href="/tag/06J9">9.4.5.4</a>, a diagram $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \mathrm{Ord}_{&lt; \kappa _0 } ) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{-}^{0}$ admits a colimit in $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{-}^{0}$ if and only if it admits a colimit in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{-}$, which case the colimits are the same (see Remark <a data-tag="06GZ" href="/tag/06GZ">9.4.1.16</a>). Condition $(\star )$ is therefore a consequence of the following stronger condition: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(\star ^{+})$</dt>
<dd><p>
There exists a regular cardinal $\kappa _0 &lt; \kappa $ for which the $\infty $-categories $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{-}$ and $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{+}$ admit $\kappa _0$-sequential colimits, and the functors $F_{-}$ and $F_{+}$ preserve $\kappa _0$-sequential colimits. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
